    }), "\n", _jsx(_components.p, {
      children: "Scalability in client-server systems is not a single property but a cluster of concerns: throughput (requests per second), latency (response time under load), availability (uptime during failures), and cost efficiency (resources consumed per request). These properties often pull in different directions, and architecture decisions made early have outsized downstream consequences."
