    }), "\n", _jsx(_components.p, {
      children: "Horizontal scaling-running multiple server instances behind a load balancer-is the standard approach for production systems. It requires that servers be stateless: any server must be able to handle any request without depending on local in-memory state from a previous request. This means sessions must live in a distributed store (Redis is the most common choice), uploaded files must be stored in object storage (S3 or compatible), and background job queues must be externalized. The statelessness constraint is not optional-it is what makes horizontal scaling work."
    }), "\n", _jsx(_components.h3, {
