      }), " A client-server API is a legal contract between two parties. REST endpoints, GraphQL schemas, and Protobuf definitions are the written terms. Versioning is the amendment process. Deprecation notices are the 30-day cancellation clause. Breaking changes without versioning are unilateral contract violations. This framing makes it clearer why API design deserves careful upfront thought: you are not just writing code, you are publishing terms that other parties will build on."]
